00:02:36.180 --> 00:02:42.930
Tanjiro's desire, his big goal is super clearly
defined and tells us a lot about his character:

00:02:42.930 --> 00:02:48.060
After his entire family is murdered, except
for his sister, who is turned into a demon,

00:02:48.060 --> 00:02:53.250
Tanjrio doeasn't seek revenge, but simply
wants to save the last remaining member of

00:02:53.250 --> 00:03:00.100
his family and turn Nezuko back into a human.
This perfectly sets up his most important

00:03:00.100 --> 00:03:06.160
character trait overall his empathy. And I
found that really interesting, because Tanjiro

00:03:06.160 --> 00:03:18.760
even is kind or at least empathetic to the
demons he encounters. He is the only one that

00:03:18.760 --> 00:03:24.950
is willing to see them as people, but at the
same time he still wants to turn Nezuko back.

00:03:24.950 --> 00:03:30.489
At first I found that a little bit paradoxical,
but when you actually think about it, it speaks

00:03:30.489 --> 00:03:36.310
of a certain maturity. He is able to see the
people who were turned into demons, but he

00:03:36.310 --> 00:03:42.940
still dislikes the condition of being a demon,
for obvious reasons, I mean they eat people

00:03:42.940 --> 00:03:43.940
and shit.

00:03:43.940 --> 00:03:49.110
Now usually, for most heroes, beneath that
superficial desire that they have, there is

00:03:49.110 --> 00:03:55.001
actually a subconscious need that a character
has. A lie they believe about the world, that

00:03:55.001 --> 00:04:00.799
needs to be challenged. Now at the beginning
of the series, it would be easy to say Tanjiro's

00:04:00.799 --> 00:04:07.140
need is to lose his naivety. You can't empathise
with everyone, especially if they are trying

00:04:07.140 --> 00:04:13.780
to kill you. It seems like his kindness and
hate for violence might be a hindrance in

00:04:13.780 --> 00:04:19.910
his fight against the most evil and strongest
beings in this world. However that is proven

00:04:19.910 --> 00:04:22.160
wrong relatively quickly.

00:04:22.160 --> 00:04:29.300
Tanjiro proves to us very early on that he
can do both, be kind and caring AND do what

00:04:29.300 --> 00:04:35.270
is necessary at the same time. He has a sort
of kind ruthlessness in him, that results

00:04:35.270 --> 00:04:49.220
in scenes like this [gently cutting the girls
head of].

00:04:49.220 --> 00:04:54.430
The point, that I found really astonishing
to be honest, is that Tanjiro doesn't really

00:04:54.430 --> 00:05:00.370
have a need to change. He is an incredibly
kind and caring person with a strong will

00:05:00.370 --> 00:05:06.990
to fight and get stronger to protect his sister
and those who need protection, and he stays

00:05:06.990 --> 00:05:12.960
that person. As a result, Tanjiro has close
to no character development in the story.

00:05:12.960 --> 00:05:19.400
Now, you probably know a few people, who proclaim
that if a character has no character development,

00:05:19.400 --> 00:05:27.560
it's a bad character. Which is not true. A
character is bad if he is inconsistent or

00:05:27.560 --> 00:05:34.490
simply boring. The reason Tanjiro stands out
as a Shounen hero however, is that most shounen

00:05:34.490 --> 00:05:40.940
protagonists have a positive character arc.
They start with a fault to their character,

00:05:40.940 --> 00:06:01.210
that they resolve at the end of the story.
They have positive character arcs, becoming

00:06:01.210 --> 00:06:07.569
better people as the story goes on. Even a
character like Saitama in One Punch Man needs

00:06:07.569 --> 00:06:12.020
to learn that true happiness doesn't come
from fighting stronger and stronger opponents,

00:06:12.020 --> 00:06:14.680
but from the relationship he has built.

00:06:14.680 --> 00:06:20.860
A rare variation on this is a negative character
arc, where the hero becomes disillusioned

00:06:20.860 --> 00:06:33.310
with the world and becomes a worse person,
like Gon in Hunter x Hunter.

00:06:33.310 --> 00:06:43.759
Tanjiro on the other hand has a flat character
arc, yup that's a real thing. He already has

00:06:43.759 --> 00:06:50.130
accepted the world as it is and has chosen
his path of how to approach it. In his case

00:06:50.130 --> 00:06:57.889
kindness. Flat arcs are very rare in Shounen,
because the audience expects the hero to grow

00:06:57.889 --> 00:07:03.291
and change as they face harder and harder
obstacles. And flat character arcs thus can

00:07:03.291 --> 00:07:10.860
be confusing or frustrating. A good example
I think is Ichigo from bleach. He also barely

00:07:10.860 --> 00:07:16.569
changes throughout the story, and only gets
stronger physically. The problem is, is that

00:07:16.569 --> 00:07:23.270
bleach is way too long for such a hero. It
becomes dull at some point, which was ultimately

00:07:23.270 --> 00:07:24.770
its downfall.

00:07:24.770 --> 00:07:29.420
Demon slayer on the other hand is relatively
short. The manga is already over, and there

00:07:29.420 --> 00:07:34.990
might be even less than 100 anime episodes
at the end, which lets us focus on the world

00:07:34.990 --> 00:07:38.830
and people around Tanjiro without it getting
too boring.

00:07:38.830 --> 00:07:44.169
That being said, flat arcs depend on your
taste, and if you prefer seeing someone grow

00:07:44.169 --> 00:07:50.759
as a person, then that's fair, I totally get
that. But it's not bad writing in Tanjiro's

00:07:50.759 --> 00:07:51.759
case.

00:07:51.759 --> 00:08:08.560
His only flaw is his physical weakness, that
he has to continually fight and struggle against.

00:08:08.560 --> 00:08:13.840
He hates how useless he is, how he cannot
help the people he wants to help.

00:08:13.840 --> 00:08:18.750
Once criticism I personally have here, is
that I feel like the characters around Tanjiro

00:08:18.750 --> 00:08:25.280
could use way stronger character arcs. I think
Tanjiro as a pillar of goodness would have

00:08:25.280 --> 00:08:30.759
actually been some really great writing if
the people around him changed a lot more in

00:08:30.759 --> 00:08:37.169
his presence than they do in the end. Shinobu
and Kanao are the closest we get, but it could

00:08:37.169 --> 00:08:40.180
have been more impactful I think.

00:08:40.180 --> 00:08:45.250
The people who change the most are the demons,
and that only after they are defeated. Which

00:08:45.250 --> 00:08:46.810
I find a bit of a shame.

00:08:46.810 --> 00:08:50.420
So what IS Tanjiro all about then?

00:08:50.420 --> 00:08:56.690
Well as most heroes, he is the foil and exact
opposite to the villain of the story, Muzan

00:08:56.690 --> 00:09:07.840
in every aspect. Everything from their motivations,
to the ideals and values they represent.

00:09:07.840 --> 00:09:13.380
While Muzan only cares about himself and sees
everyone around him, demons and humans alike

00:09:13.380 --> 00:09:19.791
as tools to use for his desires, Tanjiro’s
central defining trait is his altruism. His

00:09:19.791 --> 00:09:24.800
greatest priority will always be the lives
of other people around him. Even though he’s

00:09:24.800 --> 00:09:31.430
fighting against literal demons, he sees every
last of them as people. While he does not

00:09:31.430 --> 00:09:36.459
forgive and still condemns them for their
actions, in the end he acknowledges that all

00:09:36.459 --> 00:09:42.520
of them were humans at one point and tries
his best to respect their feelings. Even though

00:09:42.520 --> 00:09:47.279
he has to take their lives in order to protect
his own or that of his friends, he tries to

00:09:47.279 --> 00:09:52.180
give them the kindness that they were denied
during their lifetime, giving them a bit of

00:09:52.180 --> 00:10:04.209
redemption and a final chance to reflect on
their lives. And so his arc is purely about

00:10:04.209 --> 00:10:10.520
finding strength without throwing away his
kindness, or his humanity. Instead of changing

00:10:10.520 --> 00:10:19.450
and becoming a better person, Tanjiro is all
about staying the great man he is. He embodies

00:10:19.450 --> 00:10:25.470
the ideal of existentialism, basically the
idea that his life derives meaning and happiness

00:10:25.470 --> 00:10:31.640
from selflessly giving to the people around
him. To the point where he tries to give meaning

00:10:31.640 --> 00:10:34.440
to everyone he meets. [Tanjiro and the girl]

00:10:34.440 --> 00:10:39.410
Even though the first season of Demon Slayer
was an absolute firework in terms of production

00:10:39.410 --> 00:10:44.290
for me, as I explained in my previous video,
the Mugen Train movie really took me by surprise

00:10:44.290 --> 00:10:51.579
with its story line, especially for Tanjiro.
The fact that we got to physically enter everyone's

00:10:51.579 --> 00:10:57.770
deepest desire and even more interestingly,
see everyone's subconsciousness was an incredibly

00:10:57.770 --> 00:11:02.620
creative choice in my opinion. I doubt this
was on purpose, but the visual nature of the

00:11:02.620 --> 00:11:08.350
anime makes up for a lot of the character
writing in my opinion and so literally visualising

00:11:08.350 --> 00:11:12.660
everyone's personality was a really awesome
move.

00:11:12.660 --> 00:11:19.440
Touché. I wonder what my subconscious would
look like. Mostly coffee probably and you

00:11:19.440 --> 00:11:22.269
gently hitting the subscribe button.

00:11:22.269 --> 00:11:27.380
Anyways, in Tanjiro’s dream, instead of
returning back to his family left dead after

00:11:27.380 --> 00:11:38.850
being massacred, he finds them alive instead,
at least at first.

00:11:38.850 --> 00:11:47.480
Tanjiro’s desire is very simple — to just
live a happy live with with his family. After

00:11:47.480 --> 00:11:52.420
all, he’s just a simple charcoal-burner,
and a simple elder brother who became the

00:11:52.420 --> 00:11:54.732
breadwinner at a young age after the death
of his father.

00:11:54.732 --> 00:12:01.110
The dream brings to light all of his trauma,
regrets, and guilt that he must carry with

00:12:01.110 --> 00:12:07.170
him at all times, as he huggs his “alive”
siblings so tightly, apologizing over and

00:12:07.170 --> 00:12:13.990
over again, even though his dream self doesn’t
know exactly why he was apologizing and crying.

00:12:13.990 --> 00:12:19.170
Tanjiro understandably has a pretty severe
case of survivor's guilt, as he was the only

00:12:19.170 --> 00:12:30.149
one who got away unharmed, especially as the
oldest brother. It is the first time since

00:12:30.149 --> 00:12:35.520
going on his journey, where he can pause and
reflect on that fact, because he kept himself

00:12:35.520 --> 00:12:40.060
distracted with his mission to get stronger
and at least save Nezuko.

00:12:40.060 --> 00:12:45.880
At the same time it once again shows that
Tanjiro is already mature and priorities those

00:12:45.880 --> 00:12:50.700
around him. Instead of allowing himself to
be drawn in by the thing he desires most,

00:12:50.700 --> 00:12:56.260
he is able to let go of the past in order
to save the people on board of the train.

00:12:56.260 --> 00:13:01.270
He even goes so far as to kill himself in
order to get out of the dream, which is pretty

00:13:01.270 --> 00:13:03.290
radical, if I'm being honest.

00:13:03.290 --> 00:13:09.560
And yet, despite all the pain and regret inside
him, when we get to enter Tanjiro's subconsciousness,

00:13:09.560 --> 00:13:17.070
it still is an endless oasis of love and warmth,
with his core shining as bright as the sun,

00:13:17.070 --> 00:13:26.950
the thing demons fear the most. He still reminds
unconditionally kind to the point where you

00:13:26.950 --> 00:13:38.700
could call him the personification of kindness
itself. The boy who entered this place was

00:13:38.700 --> 00:13:44.670
reduced to tears and is healed from his darkness,
exactly the thing I would have liked to see

00:13:44.670 --> 00:13:50.350
for more characters around him. Tanjiro is
the sun that frees people and demons alike

00:13:50.350 --> 00:13:56.449
from the darkness of their hearts and their
eternal pain. And that's what makes him such

00:13:56.449 --> 00:13:59.010
a unique character in the shounen genre.

00:13:59.010 --> 00:14:00.010
If you want to hear my full thoughts on the
series until now, I strongly recommend you

00:14:00.010 --> 00:14:00.019
check out that video right here. Thanks for
watching.

